		(property "Design Note" "DNP, land kept (Fab, 2026-09-12). DS41326 Table 2's 2 x 22 uF is the recommendation for the 2 A part at full load; Eq.10 at THIS board's ~3 mA wants 1.3 uF (0.3 A PFM peak, 50 mV overshoot) to 9.1 uF (0.8 A peak), and one 22 uF covers that. The land stays because C3/C4 carry no MPN yet and DC-bias derating is therefore UNKNOWN -- a heavily-derated 22 uF could approach the 9.1 uF floor, and on Path A this capacitance is also the first thing standing between the buck's PFM bursts and the AFE, which reaches it through R32. Populate C4 and C8 before reaching for a bead in R32. Check the chosen part's DC-bias curve against 9.1 uF at 3.3 V" (at 177.8 43.18 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
