	(symbol
		(lib_id "Device:R")
		(at 165.1 147.32 90)
		(unit 1)
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(in_bom yes)
		(on_board yes)
		(dnp no)
		(uuid "1ceea647-ee94-5dbd-acc5-17aab2190110")
		(property "Reference" "R24" (at 160.02 139.7 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0))))
		(property "Value" "47k" (at 170.18 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify right)))
		(property "Footprint" "Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric" (at 165.1 147.32 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
		(property "Design Note" "3V3A rail monitor divider top leg, into MCU PA7/ADC_IN7. NOT 1:2 any more: R25 went 47k -> 27k on 2026-09-12, so the ratio is 27/74 and FIRMWARE is VA_MON_MV = ADC x 74/27 = 2.741 x ADC, derived by gen_hw_contract.py as O2P_HW_DIV_VA_NUM/DEN rather than written by hand. This IS the sourcing pass the old note asked for. The position was 0.1% 10k (P2TC0603D1002LNTA) only because R21/R22 once shared it, and those went with the trim and guard dividers. Nothing downstream SCALES by this reading -- it is rail health. The old note contrasted this pair with R34/R35, the 0.1% VREF_MON divider whose ratio main.c promoted into g_cyc.vref_mv: THAT DIVIDER IS DELETED and the reference is no longer measured at all, so the contrast no longer exists and this pair is simply the only rail divider left that needs no precision. 47k rather than 10k also drops the continuous draw on the analog rail feeding U4/U7 (U8 is deleted) from 165 uA to 35 uA. Source impedance went 5k -> 23.5k on that pass and is 17.2k today with the 27k bottom leg, and that is CHECKED, not assumed: ST DS12232 Table 59 (Maximum ADC RAIN) allows 50k at 12 bits and 160.5 sampling cycles, which is what mcu_adc.c already selects -- 2.9x margin at 17.2k (it was 2.1x at 23.5k), and more in practice because Table 59 is quoted at a 35 MHz ADC clock where this board runs 16 MHz. DO NOT RAISE THIS DIVIDER FURTHER: 100k legs would put the source at exactly the 50k limit. It releases the matched-pair placement adjacency the two-layer refloorplan work was holding" (at 165.1 147.32 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
		(pin "1" (uuid "8a148c7f-f9e0-50fd-a531-431e84a919b6"))
		(pin "2" (uuid "d2fcd4d5-a86c-55ed-aacc-354494ae4951"))
		(instances
			(project "o2-probe" (path "/b44d674b-6a5d-5766-ad6a-7746f68babf9" (reference "R24") (unit 1)))
		)
	)
	(symbol
		(lib_id "Device:R")
		(at 165.1 157.48 90)
		(unit 1)
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(in_bom yes)
		(on_board yes)
		(dnp no)
		(uuid "4be57e26-14dc-51e2-a19a-12990dc4579a")
		(property "Reference" "R25" (at 160.02 149.86 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0))))
		(property "Value" "27k" (at 170.18 152.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify right)))
		(property "Footprint" "Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric" (at 165.1 157.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
		(property "Design Note" "3V3A rail monitor divider bottom leg; see R24. 47k -> 27k on 2026-09-12 because the ADC full scale became 2.500 V when VREF+ moved to /VREF_TRIM. Ratio 27/74 = 0.3649, so 3.3 V reads 1.204 V and the CEILING RISES to 6.85 V -- BETTER than the 6.60 V this divider had against a 3.3 V full scale, so the rail keeps its over-range headroom rather than losing it. Source impedance also falls 23.5k -> 17.2k, further inside Table 59's 50k. FIRMWARE follows automatically: gen_hw_contract.py derives O2P_HW_DIV_VA_NUM/DEN from these two values" (at 165.1 157.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
		(pin "1" (uuid "fb710f32-16e8-56c7-aec6-54361b310ca2"))
		(pin "2" (uuid "981d8b9a-9577-59e0-a525-fe9a286a1cd7"))
		(instances
			(project "o2-probe" (path "/b44d674b-6a5d-5766-ad6a-7746f68babf9" (reference "R25") (unit 1)))
		)
	)
