		(uuid "a8fc4ee8-824f-5d3c-a73c-8cf19087e0ba")
		(property "Reference" "R45" (at 68.58 107.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0))))
		(property "Value" "47k" (at 78.74 110.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify right)))
		(property "Footprint" "Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric" (at 73.66 115.57 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
		(property "Design Note" "REV B.  The failsafe that makes the RE split SAFE, and it is the whole reason the split is not dangerous.  RE is active low with a 2 MOhm internal pull-UP, so an undriven RE pin is a DISABLED receiver -- and every MCU GPIO is high-impedance out of reset.  Without this resistor a probe that reset into the RS-485 bootloader (loader_main.c / loader_uart.c) would come up DEAF, destroying the field-reflash path SCHEMATIC-REVIEW.md M2 exists to provide.  A potted probe would be unrecoverable.  R45 makes receiver-enabled the passive default exactly as R7 makes driver-disabled the passive default.\nARITHMETIC.  Size against the GUARANTEED spec, not the 2 MOhm typical: SLLSEY3E gives IIN = +/-6.2 uA max for D, DE and RE over 3 V <= VCC <= 5.5 V, with VIL max 0.8 V.  So the largest pull-down that still guarantees a low is R <= 0.8 V / 6.2 uA = 129k.\n  47k: worst case 6.2 uA * 47k = 291 mV, a 2.75x margin to VIL.  (The 2 MOhm typical would give 76 mV, but a typical is not a guarantee and this pin must never come up deaf.)\nCOST, stated plainly because it bounds the win this split was made for: commanding standby means DRIVING RE high, which pushes 3.3 V / 47k = 70.2 uA through R45.  Standby is therefore ~70 uA, not the part's 0.1 uA.  Against the 700 uA receiver that is still a 10x cut (630 uA saved), but it is NOT the 7000x the datasheet row promises, and at the duty-cycled floor of ~29 uA in POWER-BUDGET.md this resistor would be the single largest load on the board.\nWHY NOT A WEAKER PULL-DOWN: the 129k ceiling above means no resistor can better ~26 uA, so 220k/470k do not trade margin for microamps -- they are simply OUT OF SPEC (220k worst case = 1.36 V, 470k = 2.9 V, both above VIL).  A resistor structurally cannot reach the 0.1 uA this split was made for; only omitting R45 and having the loader drive RE low early can, and that trades a sub-ms deaf window after reset.  Fab chose 47k, 2026-09-07: robust, passive, no init-order dependency." (at 73.66 115.57 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) hide))
		(pin "1" (uuid "c44e61e4-f303-5d14-a893-6a0c0d372ff7"))
